# Engine configuration. Copy to an ignored .env.local, never commit credentials.
# Run: uv run --env-file .env.local uvicorn ginseng.api:app --app-dir engine --port 8000
# Local database: bunx supabase start; bunx supabase status
# Podman users: set DOCKER_HOST=unix:///run/user/1000/podman/podman.sock for CLI calls.
# Use the SAME Supabase project in engine and web configuration.
SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321
SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
GINSENG_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173,http://127.0.0.1:5173

# Optional simulated provider; NEVER a real bank connection. Server only.
NESSIE_API_KEY=

# Optional authenticated assistant. Server only; never use a PUBLIC_ key.
# With no key, chat returns an actionable 503; the workspace still works.
# Restart the engine after changing these settings.
GEMINI_API_KEY=
GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.6-flash
# Sending shares the question, up to six recent exchanges, and relevant
# saved financial context with Google Gemini. Demo context remains synthetic.
# Personal chat can propose account/bill additions; only explicit approval saves them.
# It never moves bank money. Cash estimates cover known bills, not probabilistic reserves.
# No automatic provider retries; 20-second deadline.
# Quotas are process-local: two active requests globally, one per user,
# ten requests/minute/user. Add shared limits before running multiple workers.
# POST /chat streams application/x-ndjson: delta events, then done metadata.
# A personal done event may include a validated addition proposal and schedule preview.
# Approval uses PUT /workspace with the expected revision; conflicts require a fresh proposal.
# A terminal error or disconnect discards the partial reply from conversation history.
# Keep reverse-proxy response buffering disabled for /chat.

# Development / promotion procedure:
# 1. Start the isolated local stack; it applies supabase/migrations automatically.
# 2. Apply new migrations locally with: bunx supabase migration up --local
# 3. Run database regressions with: bunx supabase test db
# 4. Verify application behavior against local auth, then a separate staging project.
# 5. Before hosted promotion, back up and reconcile remote migration history.
#    0001 was originally applied through the dashboard; do not blindly replay it.
#    Review the migration plan and obtain approval before targeting hosted data.
# Never use db reset, test fixtures, or account-cleanup SQL on a hosted project.
